# sweep: --bare --seed-root examples/chat/fixtures/options
# The last reply offered answers to tap, and a placeholder openai key is
# installed so each network failure gets its own words. Every send happens
# under a failing scenario, so nothing leaves the simulator.
wait-for Chat
wait-for Tap an answer
expect Something short
expect A long novel
expect Poetry
expect Type something else
clean
shot options
# Typing something else raises the keyboard, says where it goes, and Back
# returns to the same answers.
tap Type something else
wait-for Type a message
expect Goes to OpenAI.
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for Tap an answer
# A tapped answer is sent as the reader's next message.
scenario offline
tap Poetry
wait-for Try again
expect This reader is not on Wi-Fi.
expect Poetry
expect-missing Tap an answer
clean
shot options-offline
# Try again resends, and each failure says what it was.
scenario host-down
tap Try again
wait-for OpenAI did not answer
expect Try again
clean
shot options-host-down
scenario network-timeout
tap Try again
wait-for OpenAI took too long to answer
expect Try again
# Save a copy with no room left says so and offers to try again.
scenario storage-full
tap more
tap Save a copy
wait-for There is not enough room left on this reader.
expect Chat conversation
clean
shot export-no-room
scenario normal
tap Try again
wait-for Ready for your computer.
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for Poetry
# The conversation and the chosen service survive a restart.
tap Service
wait-for gemini-3.6-flash
tap Google Gemini
wait-for Poetry
restart
wait-for Poetry
expect What should I read next?
tap Type
wait-for Goes to Google Gemini.
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for Poetry
clean
shot options-after-restart
# The earlier reply was written by OpenAI, and its byline keeps saying so
# after the service is changed.
expect OpenAI
